# Additive graphify excludes (node_modules/build are already auto-pruned).
# Trim monorepo noise so the graph stays focused on real source.

# Legacy webapp is kept for reference only — exclude from the graph to
# avoid confusing/stale cross-references.
apps/legacy-webapp/

dist/
build/
.next/
.turbo/
coverage/
storybook-static/
**/*.d.ts
**/*.stories.tsx
**/*.stories.ts

# package.json / lockfiles otherwise become hundreds of npm-dependency-name
# nodes (react, tailwindcss, a whole "devDependencies" community) that drown out
# real code structure in the graph. Workspace + alias resolution comes from
# pnpm-workspace.yaml and per-package tsconfig `paths`, NOT from these files, so
# excluding them keeps every cross-package edge intact. (Verified: components→ui,
# web-sdk→components, webapp→components all still resolve after this exclusion.)
**/package.json
**/package-lock.json
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/yarn.lock

# Markdown docs (upgrade/migration guides, REPO_CONTEXT.md, the .claude skill
# docs, etc.) add thousands of doc/concept nodes whose generic headings HIJACK
# natural-language queries: verified that `graphify query "how does authentication
# work"` matched a heading in docs/upgrades/UPGRADE_TESTING_CHECKLIST.md and
# returned a useless checklist, while a code-only graph resolved the same query to
# the real auth code (authentication-modal.tsx, api/auth.ts, useAuthContext). Keep
# the graph code-focused so the LLM-facing `query`/`explain`/`affected` stay useful.
# (Remove this rule if you specifically want docs indexed as a knowledge layer.)
**/*.md
